 - The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).
 
+## When beforeSession throws
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws or rejects with an `Error`, the rejection still reaches the caller and `onError` fires with `(session, error)` in the same argument shape as any other orchestrator failure ([validated by: fires onError with the session and error and still rejects when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/beforeSessionThrows.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- `afterSession` fires after `onError` when `beforeSession` throws, with `beforeUserInput`, `afterUserInput`, `beforeModelResponse`, the provider, and `afterModelResponse` never having run; a cleanup hook cannot assume `beforeSession` finished allocating and must tolerate partial or unallocated state ([validated by: fires afterSession after onError without running mid-turn hooks or the provider when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/beforeSessionThrows.acceptance.test.ts#L43)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
 These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
